 4. 🕔 After hours: The Empire cashes back 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 The Darth Vader lightsaber sold at auction. Photo: Heritage Auctions, HA.com

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The force was apparently with the auctioneers when they went to sell the lightsaber used by Darth Vader when he told Luke Skywalker, "I am your father." 

 It went for $4.875 million, marking the all-time auction record for a Star Wars collectible, Heritage Auctions said today. State of play: The lightsaber was part of a broader Star Wars auction that fetched nearly $8 million for a variety of items, including other screen-used props.

 The Vader lightsaber appeared in "Star Wars: Episode V — The Empire Strikes Back" — including the famous scene in Cloud City where Vader cuts off Skywalker's hand — as well as "Star Wars: Episode VI — Return of the Jedi." 💭 Nathan's thought bubble: I think for that much money, you should get an actual functioning lightsaber. 

 
 
